+# Composer quota bridge
+
+## 1. Existing system
+Preserve OpenCode's Solid UI; no new brand, dependencies, modal or application.
+Source: shared Progress and `packages/ui/src/actions/button/button.tsx` and CSS;
+`packages/app/src/composer/composer.tsx` owns the vertical `gap-3` stack.
+
+## 2. Color and surface
+Existing semantic `text-base`, `text-weak`, `surface-base`, `border-weak-base`,
+`border-active`, `surface-raised-base-hover` through shared components. No raw colors.
+
+## 3. Typography
+Existing sans font and `text-12-regular` metadata. Shared components preserve
+`--font-size-small` and `--line-height-large`.
+
+## 4. Layout
+Full-width inline panel before ComposerEditor; `gap-2` rows, `gap-3` sections,
+`min-w-0` and wrapping text. Composer retains scroll ownership.
+
+## 5. Primitives and states
+Shared Progress shows API remainingPercent, never estimates. No expandable details.
+An outlined close button keeps dismissal distinct from metadata. States: hidden,
+loading, success, partial error, request error, invalid arguments. Fixed localized errors.
+Authentication-required sections name the provider and keep connected providers' quotas visible.
+
+## 6. Motion
+No new animation. Scoped quota CSS disables Progress's width transition; preserve
+inherited focus behavior and reduced motion.
+
+## 7. Accessibility
+Named progress bars, live loading/error feedback, keyboard-operable close button,
+inherited focus states. Go's null 5h reset uses the official first-use label;
+other missing reset timestamps explicitly say unavailable.
+
+## 8. Accepted debt
+Solid needs no React tooling. Browser/mobile/theme visual QA and authenticated RPC
+verification remain parent-session gates; unit tests do not prove visual quality.
